248
00:20:18,000 --> 00:20:20,000
Come on, move it.

249
00:20:20,000 --> 00:20:22,000
Let's go. Come on. Up the stairs.

250
00:20:22,000 --> 00:20:24,000
Get up.

251
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:26,000
Come on, let's go.

252
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:28,000
Let's go.

253
00:20:28,000 --> 00:20:30,160
Get up the gate.

254
00:20:30,160 --> 00:20:31,960
Come on, move it.

255
00:20:31,960 --> 00:20:32,960
All right, come on.

256
00:20:32,960 --> 00:20:33,960
Move it, boy.

257
00:20:33,960 --> 00:20:35,340
Oh, yeah.

258
00:20:35,340 --> 00:20:36,640
Hey, you, go on.

259
00:20:36,640 --> 00:20:37,960
Get up.

260
00:20:37,960 --> 00:20:39,840
Sit down right there.

261
00:20:39,840 --> 00:20:42,140
Whee.

262
00:20:42,140 --> 00:20:44,680
Come on.

263
00:20:44,680 --> 00:20:45,680
Right there, sit down.

264
00:20:58,000 --> 00:20:59,000
I'm sorry.

265
00:21:23,000 --> 00:21:25,000
Cheer, and don't be so cast down.

266
00:21:28,000 --> 00:21:38,740
If you want to survive, do and say as little as possible.

267
00:21:40,680 --> 00:21:44,440
Tell no one who you really are and tell no one you can read and write.

268
00:21:47,180 --> 00:21:48,780
Unless you want to be a dead nigga.

269
00:21:58,000 --> 00:22:07,200
Now keep your mouth shut.

270
00:22:14,960 --> 00:22:16,180
I say we fight.

271
00:22:17,760 --> 00:22:19,180
The crew is fairly small.

272
00:22:20,280 --> 00:22:22,480
We're well planned. I believe they could be strong on.

273
00:22:22,620 --> 00:22:24,300
Three can't go against the whole crew.

274
00:22:25,500 --> 00:22:27,000
The rest of you are niggas.

275
00:22:28,000 --> 00:22:31,500
Born and bred slaves. Niggas ain't got no stomach for a fight.

276
00:22:31,500 --> 00:22:33,500
Not a damn one.

277
00:22:33,500 --> 00:22:35,500
Boss, I know.

278
00:22:35,500 --> 00:22:37,500
We get we were traveling.

279
00:22:37,500 --> 00:22:39,500
We wish we'd die trying.

280
00:22:39,500 --> 00:22:41,500
Survival's not about certain death.

281
00:22:41,500 --> 00:22:43,500
It's about keeping your head down.

282
00:22:47,500 --> 00:22:49,500
Days ago I was with my family.

283
00:22:51,500 --> 00:22:53,500
In my home.

284
00:22:55,000 --> 00:22:57,000
Now you tell me all is lost.

285
00:22:58,000 --> 00:23:02,000
Tell no one who I am. That's the way to survive.

286
00:23:05,000 --> 00:23:08,000
Well, I don't want to survive.

287
00:23:08,000 --> 00:23:11,000
I want to live.

288
00:23:28,000 --> 00:23:57,980
All right.

289
00:23:58,000 --> 00:24:00,000
Come on.

290
00:24:28,000 --> 00:24:42,100
Better off.

291
00:24:43,040 --> 00:24:44,860
Better than us.

292
00:24:58,000 --> 00:25:00,060
you

293
00:25:00,000 --> 00:25:03,240
I don't see him.

294
00:25:04,040 --> 00:25:06,120
Clemens! Clemens Ray!

295
00:25:06,820 --> 00:25:07,340
Clemens!

296
00:25:09,520 --> 00:25:10,760
Who's in charge here?

297
00:25:10,940 --> 00:25:11,620
I'm the captain.

298
00:25:12,020 --> 00:25:13,260
I'm Mr. Jonas Ray.

299
00:25:13,540 --> 00:25:18,040
My solicitor has documentation verifying the Negro known as Clemens Ray is my property.

300
00:25:18,120 --> 00:25:19,560
I know nothing of this arrangement.

301
00:25:20,340 --> 00:25:23,880
You are ordered to return that property immediately or be charged with thievery.

302
00:25:25,300 --> 00:25:26,000
Free him!

303
00:25:30,000 --> 00:25:32,000
Mr. Reza.

304
00:25:32,000 --> 00:25:34,000
All right, that's it.

305
00:25:34,000 --> 00:25:36,000
Clamos! Clamos!

306
00:25:36,000 --> 00:25:38,000
Get him back!

307
00:25:38,000 --> 00:25:40,000
Clamos! Clamos!

308
00:25:40,000 --> 00:25:42,000
Clamos!

309
00:26:00,000 --> 00:26:29,980
I'm sorry.

310
00:26:30,000 --> 00:26:31,500
There's no dance.

311
00:26:47,760 --> 00:26:48,760
Mr. Parker.

312
00:26:48,760 --> 00:26:51,060
Ah, Mr. Northup.

313
00:26:51,060 --> 00:26:52,600
Mrs. Northup.

314
00:26:52,600 --> 00:26:54,820
Solomon, can I interest you in a new crew bag?

315
00:26:54,820 --> 00:26:56,160
Pure silk by way of the French.

316
00:26:56,160 --> 00:26:57,700
We're in need of a fresh carry-off.

317
00:26:57,700 --> 00:26:59,080
My missus is Travis.

318
00:26:59,080 --> 00:27:00,080
Nothing more.

319
00:27:00,080 --> 00:27:02,080
The year has passed already.

320
00:27:02,080 --> 00:27:03,080
Off to work at Sandy Hill again?

321
00:27:03,080 --> 00:27:04,080
I am.

322
00:27:04,080 --> 00:27:06,080
I have just the thing.

323
00:27:06,080 --> 00:27:10,080
Something to suit your style and yet sturdy enough for the 40-mile round trip.

324
00:27:10,080 --> 00:27:11,080
It's beautiful.

325
00:27:11,080 --> 00:27:12,080
At what price?

326
00:27:12,080 --> 00:27:13,080
We will take it.

327
00:27:13,080 --> 00:27:16,080
Children, come see what your father has just purchased for me.

328
00:27:16,080 --> 00:27:17,080
One moment, sir.

329
00:27:17,080 --> 00:27:18,080
You'll be assisted.

330
00:27:18,080 --> 00:27:19,080
Mr. Parker.

331
00:27:19,080 --> 00:27:20,080
Sir.

332
00:27:20,080 --> 00:27:21,080
If we could discuss the price.

333
00:27:21,080 --> 00:27:22,080
Forgive me, Solomon.

334
00:27:22,080 --> 00:27:24,080
Mrs. Northup, a customer waits.

335
00:27:24,080 --> 00:27:25,080
Welcome, sir.

336
00:27:25,080 --> 00:27:27,080
Shop well, sir, but mind your wallet.

337
00:27:27,080 --> 00:27:29,080
Hey, no attention to this gentleman's nonsense.

338
00:27:29,080 --> 00:27:31,080
Jesper!

339
00:27:31,080 --> 00:27:34,080
My regrets for the intrusion, sir.

340
00:27:34,080 --> 00:27:36,080
No intrusion.

341
00:27:39,080 --> 00:27:41,080
Good day, sir.

342
00:27:41,080 --> 00:27:43,080
Good day.

343
00:27:43,080 --> 00:27:45,080
Jesper.

344
00:27:53,080 --> 00:27:55,080
Very good, very good.

345
00:27:55,080 --> 00:27:57,580
Let's see here. Eliza!

346
00:27:58,880 --> 00:28:01,260
Stand up when you hear your name. Eliza.

347
00:28:02,920 --> 00:28:03,340
Leffy.

348
00:28:06,520 --> 00:28:07,580
John.

349
00:28:09,420 --> 00:28:10,000
Oren.

350
00:28:12,020 --> 00:28:12,420
Platt.

351
00:28:15,440 --> 00:28:16,480
Platt.

352
00:28:19,860 --> 00:28:21,080
Stand up.

353
00:28:21,080 --> 00:28:26,580
You fit the description given. Why didn't you answer when called?

354
00:28:26,580 --> 00:28:28,580
My name's not Platt. My name...

355
00:28:31,080 --> 00:28:33,080
Your name is Platt.

356
00:28:35,080 --> 00:28:37,080
Captain, get these niggers to my cart.

357
00:28:51,080 --> 00:29:07,580
I believe I have something very much to your liking in the back room.

358
00:29:08,080 --> 00:29:09,060
Follow me, please.

359
00:29:10,000 --> 00:29:10,500
Yes.

360
00:29:11,500 --> 00:29:12,840
Inspect them at your leisure.

361
00:29:12,840 --> 00:29:17,540
But I ask you to pay particular regard to young Ezra here.

362
00:29:17,920 --> 00:29:19,200
Incredibly sound limbs.

363
00:29:19,200 --> 00:29:21,240
I have never seen anything quite like him.

364
00:29:21,240 --> 00:29:23,740
And this marvelous creature, can you believe it?

365
00:29:23,740 --> 00:29:24,740
Hmm?

366
00:29:24,740 --> 00:29:26,000
She'll make a fine lady's maid.

367
00:29:26,000 --> 00:29:27,040
Yes, madam.

368
00:29:27,040 --> 00:29:29,620
So inspect at your leisure.

369
00:29:29,620 --> 00:29:31,920
Take your time, help yourself to refreshments.

370
00:29:31,920 --> 00:29:34,680
Gentlemen, what catches your fancy here?

371
00:29:34,680 --> 00:29:36,220
Hmm? This boy?

372
00:29:36,220 --> 00:29:37,560
Yes, open your mouth.

373
00:29:37,560 --> 00:29:38,920
Open, wider.

374
00:29:38,920 --> 00:29:39,920
Look in there.

375
00:29:39,920 --> 00:29:41,560
Never been sick a day in his life.

376
00:29:41,560 --> 00:29:43,400
And I call particular attention to Martha.

377
00:29:43,400 --> 00:29:45,400
She is an excellent pastry cook.

378
00:29:45,400 --> 00:29:47,900
Ah, Mr. Ford.

379
00:29:47,900 --> 00:29:52,400
Splendid seeing you, sir. What catches your fancy? This lad is very brawny.

380
00:29:52,400 --> 00:29:55,400
How much are the wands, Platt and Eliza?

381
00:29:55,400 --> 00:29:58,900
Ah, yes. A thousand for Platt.

382
00:29:58,900 --> 00:29:59,900
Uh-oh.

383
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:02,940
This is a nigger of considerable talent, I assure you.

384
00:30:02,940 --> 00:30:04,840
700 for Eliza?

385
00:30:04,840 --> 00:30:05,780
My fairest price?

386
00:30:08,920 --> 00:30:10,080
You will accept a note?

387
00:30:10,080 --> 00:30:10,980
Please, sir.

388
00:30:10,980 --> 00:30:11,880
Of course, from you, Mr. Ford.

389
00:30:11,880 --> 00:30:12,900
Do not divide my family.

390
00:30:12,900 --> 00:30:14,280
Do not take me unless you take my choice.

391
00:30:14,280 --> 00:30:15,540
Eliza, quiet!

392
00:30:15,540 --> 00:30:17,380
You will have the most faithful slave in me,

393
00:30:17,380 --> 00:30:18,960
the most faithful slave that has ever lived.

394
00:30:18,960 --> 00:30:20,440
But I beg that you do not separate us.

395
00:30:20,440 --> 00:30:21,860
Your price for the boy?

396
00:30:21,860 --> 00:30:22,760
Please.

397
00:30:22,760 --> 00:30:24,060
I will give you something to cry about.

398
00:30:24,060 --> 00:30:25,040
Randall, come forward.

399
00:30:25,040 --> 00:30:26,560
Come, come, come, come, come.

400
00:30:26,560 --> 00:30:28,240
Now, you see how fit this boy is?

401
00:30:28,240 --> 00:30:30,000
You know, like ripe fruit.

402
00:30:30,080 --> 00:30:32,320
May I take your stick? A moment?

403
00:30:32,400 --> 00:30:35,120
Observe this, Randall. Jump, jump, jump, run, run.

404
00:30:35,200 --> 00:30:37,520
Very good. Higher.

405
00:30:37,600 --> 00:30:42,320
Do you see this? Very likely, he will grow into a fine beast.

406
00:30:42,400 --> 00:30:45,440
Ah, 600 for the boy.

407
00:30:45,520 --> 00:30:47,600
Fair and final.

408
00:30:47,680 --> 00:30:48,920
Done.

409
00:30:49,000 --> 00:30:51,520
Superb. A moment, please.

410
00:30:51,600 --> 00:30:53,000
Mr. Ford.

411
00:30:53,080 --> 00:30:54,400
Please. Eliza!

412
00:30:54,480 --> 00:30:56,080
How much for the little girl?

413
00:30:56,080 --> 00:31:01,080
You have no use for her. One so young will bring you no profit.

414
00:31:01,080 --> 00:31:03,080
No, no, no, no. I cannot sell the girl.

415
00:31:03,080 --> 00:31:06,080
There's heaps and piles of money to be made from her.

416
00:31:06,080 --> 00:31:09,080
She's a beauty, one of the regular bloods.

417
00:31:09,080 --> 00:31:12,080
No, none of you thick-lipped, bullet-headed, cotton-picking niggers here.

418
00:31:12,080 --> 00:31:14,080
Child, man.

419
00:31:16,080 --> 00:31:18,080
For God's sake, you're not sentimental at least.

420
00:31:18,080 --> 00:31:22,080
My sentimentality extends the length of a coin.

421
00:31:22,080 --> 00:31:27,080
Now do you take this lot? Mr. Fordow, do you pass on them all?

422
00:31:27,080 --> 00:31:30,080
Please, please, please.

423
00:31:30,080 --> 00:31:32,080
I will take the wands, plait and the lice.

424
00:31:32,080 --> 00:31:34,080
It's all the lice and the plaits, Gwendolyn.

425
00:31:34,080 --> 00:31:37,080
You will not take them from me!

426
00:31:37,080 --> 00:31:39,080
Get around her!

427
00:31:39,080 --> 00:31:41,080
Please, please, no!

428
00:31:41,080 --> 00:31:43,080
No, please!

429
00:31:43,080 --> 00:31:45,080
No!

430
00:31:45,080 --> 00:31:47,080
That's not me!

431
00:31:47,080 --> 00:31:50,080
I will keep reserving the cry about your goddamn wands!

432
00:31:50,080 --> 00:31:52,580
Get out of here, kid! Out, now! Now!

433
00:31:59,080 --> 00:32:00,080
Mr. Ford.

434
00:32:01,080 --> 00:32:02,080
Pleasure.

435
00:32:02,080 --> 00:32:19,740
Did you bring all those niggers?

436
00:32:20,700 --> 00:32:21,440
Two of them.

437
00:32:22,160 --> 00:32:23,020
You got two.

438
00:32:23,540 --> 00:32:24,340
Mr. Chapin.

439
00:32:25,360 --> 00:32:26,220
This one's crying.

440
00:32:27,100 --> 00:32:28,160
Why is this one crying?

441
00:32:28,380 --> 00:32:29,460
Separated from her children.

442
00:32:29,540 --> 00:32:30,300
Oh, dear.

443
00:32:30,540 --> 00:32:31,240
Couldn't be helped.

444
00:32:31,240 --> 00:32:33,000
Poor poor woman.

445
00:32:33,000 --> 00:32:33,820
Mr. Chapin.

446
00:32:33,820 --> 00:32:34,720
Yes, sir.

447
00:32:34,720 --> 00:32:36,160
Tomorrow you can take these two up to the mill,

448
00:32:36,160 --> 00:32:37,660
start them working.

449
00:32:37,660 --> 00:32:38,980
For now, make the matter quick.

450
00:32:38,980 --> 00:32:41,060
Fix him a meal and have him rest himself.

451
00:32:41,060 --> 00:32:43,100
Yes, sir.

452
00:32:43,100 --> 00:32:44,860
Come on now.

453
00:32:44,860 --> 00:32:45,760
Come on.

454
00:32:45,760 --> 00:32:47,340
Don't dawdle.

455
00:32:47,340 --> 00:32:50,140
Something to eat and some rest.

456
00:32:50,140 --> 00:32:51,360
Your children will soon be forgotten.

457
00:33:01,240 --> 00:33:21,040
Now, for all of you raw niggers that don't know,

458
00:33:21,140 --> 00:33:22,520
my name is John Tibby,

459
00:33:22,760 --> 00:33:24,900
William Ford's chief carpenter.

460
00:33:25,560 --> 00:33:28,120
You will refer to me as Master.

461
00:33:29,080 --> 00:33:30,260
Now, Mr. Chapin,

462
00:33:30,260 --> 00:33:32,920
is the overseer on this plantation.

463
00:33:33,200 --> 00:33:37,020
You two will refer to him as master.

464
00:33:38,500 --> 00:33:39,740
So clap your hands.

465
00:33:43,940 --> 00:33:44,900
Like this.

466
00:33:46,000 --> 00:33:46,780
Come on.

467
00:33:47,520 --> 00:33:49,160
Come on, now. Clap your hands.

468
00:33:54,000 --> 00:33:56,300
Nigger run, nigger flew,

469
00:33:56,680 --> 00:33:58,780
nigger tore his shirt in two.

470
00:33:58,780 --> 00:34:01,600
Run, run, the paddy roller'll get you

471
00:34:01,600 --> 00:34:03,880
Run, nigga, run, well, you better get away

472
00:34:03,880 --> 00:34:10,020
That's right, like you mean it

473
00:34:10,020 --> 00:34:13,500
Nigga run, run so fast

474
00:34:13,500 --> 00:34:15,700
Stove his head in a hornet's nest

475
00:34:15,700 --> 00:34:18,400
Run, run, the paddy roller'll get you

476
00:34:18,400 --> 00:34:20,560
Run, nigga, run, well, you better get away

477
00:34:20,560 --> 00:34:24,220
Run, nigga, run, the paddy roller'll get you

478
00:34:24,220 --> 00:34:26,460
Run, nigga, run, well, you better get away

479
00:34:26,460 --> 00:34:30,680
Some folks say a nigger don't steal

480
00:34:30,680 --> 00:34:32,800
I caught three in my cornfield

481
00:34:32,800 --> 00:34:35,140
One has a butcher and one has a pack

482
00:34:35,140 --> 00:34:37,560
One has a rope, it was hung around his neck

483
00:34:37,560 --> 00:34:39,680
Run, nigger, run, the patty roller

484
00:34:39,680 --> 00:34:42,320
Catch you, run, nigger, run, well, you better get away

485
00:34:42,320 --> 00:34:44,420
Run, nigger, run, the patty roller

486
00:34:44,420 --> 00:34:47,220
Catch you, run, nigger, run, well, you better get away

487
00:34:47,220 --> 00:34:50,320
Hey, Mr. Patty Roller, don't catch me

488
00:34:50,320 --> 00:34:52,780
Catch that nigger behind that tree

489
00:34:52,780 --> 00:34:54,780
Run, nigger, run, the patty roller

490
00:35:00,000 --> 00:35:02,000
Run, nigger, run, well, you better get away.

491
00:35:02,000 --> 00:35:04,500
Run, nigger, run, the patty roller'll catch you.

492
00:35:04,500 --> 00:35:07,000
Run, nigger, run, well, you better get away.

493
00:35:07,000 --> 00:35:10,000
I am the God of Abraham, the God of Isaac,

494
00:35:10,000 --> 00:35:11,500
and the God of Jacob.

495
00:35:11,500 --> 00:35:13,500
Run, nigger, run, the patty roller'll catch you.

496
00:35:13,500 --> 00:35:15,000
And when the multitude heard this,

497
00:35:15,000 --> 00:35:17,500
they were astonished at his doctrine.

498
00:35:17,500 --> 00:35:19,000
Run, nigger, run, well, you better get away.

499
00:35:19,000 --> 00:35:22,000
And then one of them, which was a lawyer,

500
00:35:22,000 --> 00:35:24,000
asked him a question, tempting him.

501
00:35:24,000 --> 00:35:28,000
Run, nigger, run, the patty roller'll catch you.

502
00:35:28,000 --> 00:35:30,000
Run, nigga, run away from me, baby.

503
00:35:58,000 --> 00:36:23,060
The creek is plenty deep enough to sail,

504
00:36:24,180 --> 00:36:25,600
even with a boat full of load.

505
00:36:25,600 --> 00:36:29,000
The distance from the work area to the point on the latter bayou

506
00:36:29,000 --> 00:36:30,880
is several miles by water fewer than land.

507
00:36:30,940 --> 00:36:32,780
It occurs to me that the expense of transportation

508
00:36:32,780 --> 00:36:34,340
would be materially diminished.

509
00:36:34,540 --> 00:36:35,460
Materially diminished?

510
00:36:35,560 --> 00:36:36,640
If we use the waterway.

511
00:36:37,440 --> 00:36:39,520
Are you an engineer or a nigger?

512
00:36:42,520 --> 00:36:44,240
Are you an engineer or a nigger?

513
00:36:46,380 --> 00:36:47,780
Let the man say his piece.

514
00:36:47,800 --> 00:36:48,580
It's a scheme.

515
00:36:49,040 --> 00:36:51,420
Plenty of engineers have schemed similarly.

516
00:36:51,560 --> 00:36:53,220
The passes are too tight.

517
00:36:53,220 --> 00:36:57,220
I reckon them are more than 12 feet at their most narrow.

518
00:36:57,220 --> 00:37:00,220
Wide enough for a tub to traverse if a team of niggers cleared it out.

519
00:37:00,220 --> 00:37:03,220
And you know what of transporting terraformin'?

520
00:37:03,220 --> 00:37:08,220
I labored repairing the Champlain Canal on the section over which William Van Nortwyk was superintendent.

521
00:37:08,220 --> 00:37:11,220
With my earnings, I hired several efficient hands to assist me,

522
00:37:11,220 --> 00:37:16,220
and ended into contracts for the transportation of large rafts of timber from Lake Champlain to Troy.

523
00:37:19,220 --> 00:37:22,220
Well, I'll admit to being impressed even if you won't.

524
00:37:22,220 --> 00:37:26,300
Well, collect the team and see what good you can do.

525
00:37:30,780 --> 00:37:35,440
When I saw you, I saw you.

526
00:37:35,440 --> 00:37:36,880
All right, keep it up.

527
00:37:36,880 --> 00:37:39,340
Two, three, four.

528
00:37:39,340 --> 00:37:42,740
For me, too late.

529
00:37:42,740 --> 00:37:47,740
For me, I'd live or die.

530
00:37:47,740 --> 00:37:51,040
Lay down and cry.

531
00:37:51,040 --> 00:37:57,040
Hey, boy, I'm proud, my lord, so proud.

532
00:37:57,040 --> 00:38:00,460
I'm strong, yes, sir.

533
00:38:00,640 --> 00:38:04,040
I'm tall, yes, sir.

534
00:38:04,380 --> 00:38:09,040
My lord, my lord, my lord.

535
00:38:10,000 --> 00:38:11,440
But you are a marvel.

536
00:38:12,820 --> 00:38:15,720
My lord, my lord, my lord.

537
00:38:15,980 --> 00:38:18,780
We're high, too high.

538
00:38:19,380 --> 00:38:20,880
What took you so long?

539
00:38:21,040 --> 00:38:23,040
Thank you, Master Voight.

540
00:38:23,040 --> 00:38:25,040
Oh, thank you.

541
00:38:25,040 --> 00:38:27,040
Yeah.

542
00:38:27,040 --> 00:38:29,040
Yes, sir.

543
00:38:29,040 --> 00:38:31,040
Yeah.

544
00:38:31,040 --> 00:38:33,040
I'll be happy.

545
00:38:33,040 --> 00:38:35,040
Come on.

546
00:38:35,040 --> 00:38:37,040
Oh, that's a wonderful thing to do.

547
00:38:41,040 --> 00:38:43,040
It's flat.

548
00:38:51,040 --> 00:39:04,040
My great thanks, Master Ford.

549
00:39:04,760 --> 00:39:05,880
My thanks to you.

550
00:39:06,780 --> 00:39:08,080
It is the least of it.

551
00:39:09,460 --> 00:39:12,040
I hope it brings us both much joy over the years.

552
00:39:21,040 --> 00:39:21,940
Yeah.

553
00:39:23,940 --> 00:39:25,940
Thank you, Matthew.

554
00:39:39,600 --> 00:39:44,600
Oh, God.

555
00:39:44,600 --> 00:39:45,500
Wait.

556
00:39:49,100 --> 00:39:50,000
Eliza.

557
00:39:51,040 --> 00:39:56,280
Eliza.

558
00:39:57,280 --> 00:39:58,240
Stop!

559
00:39:59,020 --> 00:39:59,680
Stop!

560
00:40:00,000 --> 00:40:07,060
You let yourself be overcome by sorrow, you will drown in it.

561
00:40:07,060 --> 00:40:10,540
Have you stopped crying for your children?

562
00:40:10,540 --> 00:40:14,460
You make no sounds, but will you ever let them go in your heart?

563
00:40:14,460 --> 00:40:20,240
They are as my flesh.

564
00:40:20,240 --> 00:40:23,060
Then who is distressed?

565
00:40:23,060 --> 00:40:25,560
Do I upset the master and the mistress?

566
00:40:25,560 --> 00:40:28,240
You care less about my loss than their well-being?

567
00:40:28,240 --> 00:40:29,240
Master Ford is a decent man.

568
00:40:29,240 --> 00:40:30,540
He is a slaver!

569
00:40:30,540 --> 00:40:31,540
Under the circumstances.

570
00:40:31,540 --> 00:40:33,820
Under the circumstances, he's a slaver.

571
00:40:33,820 --> 00:40:35,240
But you truckle at his boot.

572
00:40:35,240 --> 00:40:35,580
No.

573
00:40:35,580 --> 00:40:37,340
You luxuriate in his favor.

574
00:40:37,340 --> 00:40:39,540
I survive!

575
00:40:39,540 --> 00:40:41,620
I will not fall into despair.

576
00:40:41,620 --> 00:40:43,760
I will offer up my talents to Master Ford.

577
00:40:43,760 --> 00:40:46,460
I will keep myself hearty till freedom is opportune.

578
00:40:46,460 --> 00:40:49,500
Oh, Ford is your opportunity?

579
00:40:49,500 --> 00:40:52,560
You think he does not know that you are more than you suggest?

580
00:40:52,560 --> 00:40:54,400
But he does nothing for you.

581
00:40:54,400 --> 00:40:56,220
Nothing.

582
00:40:56,220 --> 00:41:00,020
You are no better than prized livestock.

583
00:41:00,020 --> 00:41:01,100
Call for him.

584
00:41:01,100 --> 00:41:02,000
Call.

585
00:41:02,000 --> 00:41:03,220
Tell him of your previous circumstances

586
00:41:03,220 --> 00:41:07,540
and see what it earns you, Solomon.

587
00:41:07,540 --> 00:41:12,000
So you settle into your role as Platt then?

588
00:41:12,000 --> 00:41:18,240
My back is thick with scars for protesting my freedom.

589
00:41:18,240 --> 00:41:19,640
Do not accuse me.

590
00:41:19,640 --> 00:41:24,280
I accuse you of nothing I cannot accuse.

591
00:41:24,280 --> 00:41:27,320
I have done dishonorable things to survive,

592
00:41:27,320 --> 00:41:29,780
and for all of them I have ended up here.

593
00:41:30,920 --> 00:41:33,360
No better than if I had stood up for myself.

594
00:41:34,500 --> 00:41:35,820
God forgive me.

595
00:41:36,960 --> 00:41:39,160
Solomon, let me weep for my children.

596
00:41:39,160 --> 00:42:05,860
I can't help that kind of depression about.

597
00:42:05,860 --> 00:42:08,320
But whoso shall offend one of these little ones,

598
00:42:08,320 --> 00:42:11,560
it were better for him that a millstone were hanged

599
00:42:11,560 --> 00:42:13,540
about his neck and he were drowned

600
00:42:13,540 --> 00:42:14,900
in the depth of the sea.

601
00:42:17,280 --> 00:42:18,100
Amen.

602
00:42:32,820 --> 00:42:34,320
Make them boards flush.

603
00:42:34,320 --> 00:42:35,820
They are, sir.

604
00:42:35,820 --> 00:42:37,820
Now, they is no such thing.

605
00:42:39,820 --> 00:42:42,820
They're as smooth to the touch as a yearling's coat.

606
00:42:45,320 --> 00:42:47,820
Why are you calling me a liar, boy?

607
00:42:50,320 --> 00:42:52,820
That's all a matter of perspective, sir.

608
00:42:52,820 --> 00:42:55,320
From where you stand, you may see differently,

609
00:42:55,320 --> 00:42:57,320
but the hands are not mistaken.

610
00:42:57,320 --> 00:42:59,820
I simply ask that you use all your senses

611
00:42:59,820 --> 00:43:01,820
before rendering judgment.

612
00:43:01,820 --> 00:43:05,820
Oh, my, you are a brute.

613
00:43:05,820 --> 00:43:07,820
You are a dog.

614
00:43:07,820 --> 00:43:11,820
And no better for following instruction!

615
00:43:11,820 --> 00:43:13,820
I'll do as ordered.

616
00:43:13,820 --> 00:43:15,820
Well, then you'll be up at daybreak.

617
00:43:15,820 --> 00:43:18,820
You'll procure a keg of nails from Chapin

618
00:43:18,820 --> 00:43:20,820
and commence to putting on clabberts.

619
00:43:20,820 --> 00:43:22,820
Yes, sir.

620
00:43:26,820 --> 00:43:29,820
Make them boards flush.

621
00:43:31,820 --> 00:43:42,160
Please, please, please say, where am I going?

622
00:43:42,160 --> 00:43:43,540
Where am I going?

623
00:43:43,840 --> 00:43:45,020
Say, Solomon!

624
00:43:45,560 --> 00:43:46,340
Solomon!

625
00:43:47,020 --> 00:43:48,020
Solomon!

626
00:43:49,300 --> 00:43:50,340
Solomon!

627
00:43:54,580 --> 00:43:55,620
Solomon!

628
00:44:01,820 --> 00:44:05,120
When I say I had my master's favor, you understand.

629
00:44:08,000 --> 00:44:11,460
And for nine years, he blessed me with every comfort

630
00:44:11,460 --> 00:44:14,900
and luxury in life, silks and jewels

631
00:44:14,900 --> 00:44:18,100
and even servants to wait upon us.

632
00:44:20,640 --> 00:44:21,960
Such was our life.

633
00:44:23,400 --> 00:44:25,460
And the life of this beautiful girl I bore for him.

634
00:44:29,120 --> 00:44:30,700
My master Barry's daughter.

635
00:44:31,820 --> 00:44:34,820
She always looked at me with an unkind nature.

636
00:44:34,820 --> 00:44:36,820
And she hated Emily,

637
00:44:36,820 --> 00:44:39,820
no matter she and Emily were flesh or flesh.

638
00:44:42,820 --> 00:44:45,820
As Master Barry's health failed, she gained power in the household,

639
00:44:45,820 --> 00:44:47,820
and eventually I was brought to the city

640
00:44:47,820 --> 00:44:51,820
under the false pretense of our free papers being executed.

641
00:44:55,820 --> 00:44:57,820
My poor children.

642
00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:29,980
I love you.

643
00:45:30,000 --> 00:45:39,980
I thought I told you to commence the putting on clappers.

644
00:45:41,680 --> 00:45:42,780
Yes, master, I'm about it.

645
00:45:42,800 --> 00:45:43,780
These have all been replaced.

646
00:45:45,680 --> 00:45:47,260
Well, didn't I tell you to get a keg of nails?

647
00:45:48,140 --> 00:45:48,840
And so I did.

648
00:45:50,500 --> 00:45:51,260
So you did.

649
00:45:52,900 --> 00:45:53,880
God damn you.

650
00:45:53,980 --> 00:45:55,640
I thought you knowed something.

651
00:45:55,640 --> 00:45:56,820
I did as instructed.

652
00:45:57,400 --> 00:45:59,960
If there's something wrong, it's wrong with the instruction.

653
00:46:00,000 --> 00:46:02,340
You black bastard.

654
00:46:02,340 --> 00:46:08,140
You goddamn black bastard.

655
00:46:08,140 --> 00:46:10,140
Strip your clothes.

656
00:46:12,140 --> 00:46:14,140
Strip.

657
00:46:14,140 --> 00:46:16,140
I will not.

658
00:46:24,140 --> 00:46:28,140
You will not live to see me.

659
00:46:30,000 --> 00:46:32,500
I'll see you another day, nigga!

660
00:46:32,500 --> 00:46:34,500
Oh, God, help!

661
00:46:34,500 --> 00:46:36,500
Oh, shit!

662
00:46:36,500 --> 00:46:38,500
Oh, God, help!

663
00:46:38,500 --> 00:46:40,500
Help!

664
00:46:40,500 --> 00:46:42,500
Murder!

665
00:46:42,500 --> 00:46:44,500
Oh, shit!

666
00:46:44,500 --> 00:46:46,500
Oh, God!

667
00:46:46,500 --> 00:46:48,500
Oh, shit!

668
00:46:48,500 --> 00:46:50,500
Oh, God!

669
00:46:50,500 --> 00:46:52,500
What does it matter?

670
00:46:52,500 --> 00:46:54,500
What does it matter?

671
00:46:54,500 --> 00:46:56,500
Master Tibbies wants to whoop me

672
00:46:56,500 --> 00:46:58,500
for using the nails you gave me.

673
00:46:58,500 --> 00:47:01,260
They say, don't buy half.

674
00:47:02,060 --> 00:47:03,680
I will have flesh.

675
00:47:04,500 --> 00:47:06,480
And I will have all of it.

676
00:47:10,380 --> 00:47:11,500
Do not stir.

677
00:47:12,200 --> 00:47:15,260
Do not leave the plantation, for if you run, I cannot protect you.

678
00:47:16,260 --> 00:47:16,960
Stay here.

679
00:47:28,500 --> 00:47:58,480
I love you.

680
00:47:58,500 --> 00:48:24,520
Gentlemen, whoever moves that nigger's a dead man.

681
00:48:24,520 --> 00:48:29,240
I am the overseer on this plantation.

682
00:48:30,000 --> 00:48:32,400
William Ford holds the mortgage on Platt.

683
00:48:32,940 --> 00:48:35,600
If you hang him, he will lose his debt.

684
00:48:35,960 --> 00:48:37,880
You have no claim to his life.

685
00:48:38,620 --> 00:48:43,080
As for you two, if you have any regard for your own safety,

686
00:48:43,840 --> 00:48:44,760
I say be gone!

687
00:48:48,120 --> 00:48:49,960
You got no cause!

688
00:48:50,420 --> 00:48:53,700
The plot is mine, and mine to do with as I please!

689
00:48:53,700 --> 00:48:54,660
You touch.

690
00:49:22,340 --> 00:49:22,860
Sam!

691
00:49:23,700 --> 00:49:26,200
Master Mew, get Master Ford!

692
00:49:53,700 --> 00:50:23,680
Thank you.

693
00:50:00,000 --> 00:50:29,980
Thank you.

694
00:50:30,000 --> 00:50:59,980
Thank you.

695
00:51:00,000 --> 00:51:29,980
All right.

696
00:51:30,000 --> 00:51:59,980
I'm sorry.

697
00:52:00,000 --> 00:52:02,000
Get down.

698
00:52:30,000 --> 00:52:55,420
I believe Tilly's just skulking about the premises somewhere.

699
00:52:55,420 --> 00:52:58,800
He wants you dead, and he will have it so.

700
00:52:58,800 --> 00:53:01,300
It's no longer safe for you here.

701
00:53:01,300 --> 00:53:05,260
I don't believe you will remain passive if Tibby's attacked.

702
00:53:05,260 --> 00:53:08,520
I have transferred my debt to Edwin Epps.

703
00:53:08,520 --> 00:53:09,520
He will take charge.

704
00:53:25,420 --> 00:53:32,020
Master Ford.

705
00:53:34,960 --> 00:53:37,820
You must know that I'm not a slave.

706
00:53:38,200 --> 00:53:39,460
I cannot hear that.

707
00:53:39,500 --> 00:53:41,720
Before I came to you, I was a free man.

708
00:53:41,760 --> 00:53:43,200
Trying to save your life.

709
00:53:45,280 --> 00:53:48,160
And I have a debt to be mindful of.

710
00:53:50,300 --> 00:53:52,280
And that is to Edwin Epps now.

711
00:53:52,280 --> 00:53:55,280
He's a hard man, prides himself on being a nigger breaker,

712
00:53:55,280 --> 00:53:58,280
but truthfully, I could find no others who would take him.

713
00:53:58,280 --> 00:54:01,280
You made a reputation of yourself.

714
00:54:01,280 --> 00:54:06,280
Whatever the circumstances, you are an exceptional nigger, Platt.

715
00:54:08,280 --> 00:54:11,280
But I fear no good will come of it.

716
00:54:22,280 --> 00:54:39,520
And that servant which knew his Lord's will,

717
00:54:39,520 --> 00:54:44,180
which knew his Lord's will,

718
00:54:44,180 --> 00:54:50,880
and prepared not himself

719
00:54:50,880 --> 00:54:55,220
prepared not himself

720
00:55:00,000 --> 00:55:02,000
neither did according to his will,

721
00:55:04,580 --> 00:55:07,800
shall be beaten with many stripes.

722
00:55:09,180 --> 00:55:10,100
Did you hear that?

723
00:55:11,220 --> 00:55:12,140
Stripes.

724
00:55:13,940 --> 00:55:16,060
That nigger that don't obey his lord,

725
00:55:16,060 --> 00:55:17,560
that's his master, do you see?

726
00:55:18,980 --> 00:55:23,240
That there nigger shall be beaten with many stripes.

727
00:55:25,280 --> 00:55:27,980
Now many signifies a great many.

728
00:55:27,980 --> 00:55:32,980
40, 100, 150 lashes.

729
00:55:37,980 --> 00:55:39,980
That's scripture.

730
00:55:39,980 --> 00:55:54,120
Oh, my God.

731
00:55:56,120 --> 00:55:57,000
Pick that gun.

732
00:55:57,940 --> 00:55:58,820
Move along now.

733
00:56:01,680 --> 00:56:02,660
Come on, Redwood.

734
00:56:03,860 --> 00:56:04,600
Drive them.

735
00:56:04,880 --> 00:56:05,820
Pick that gun.

736
00:56:06,660 --> 00:56:07,580
Move along now.

737
00:56:07,580 --> 00:56:10,580
What are you doing, boy? Come on!

738
00:56:13,580 --> 00:56:15,580
240 for Bob.

739
00:56:15,580 --> 00:56:17,580
What you got for James?

740
00:56:17,580 --> 00:56:20,580
295 pounds.

741
00:56:20,580 --> 00:56:23,580
That's real good, boy. That's real good.

742
00:56:23,580 --> 00:56:26,580
182 for Platt.

743
00:56:26,580 --> 00:56:30,580
How much can even an average nigga pick a day?

744
00:56:30,580 --> 00:56:32,580
200 pounds.

745
00:56:32,580 --> 00:56:34,580
This nigga ain't even average.

746
00:56:34,580 --> 00:56:38,620
512 pounds for Patsy.

747
00:56:38,620 --> 00:56:41,620
512!

748
00:56:41,620 --> 00:56:45,620
Your menfolk got no shame letting Patsy out pick you.

749
00:56:45,620 --> 00:56:50,620
They ain't yet come, she swung lower than 500 pounds.

750
00:56:54,620 --> 00:56:56,620
Queen of the field she is.

751
00:56:56,620 --> 00:56:58,620
138 pounds.

752
00:56:58,620 --> 00:57:00,620
I ain't done, Treech.

753
00:57:00,620 --> 00:57:04,620
Ain't I owed a minute to luxury aid on the work Patsy done?

754
00:57:04,620 --> 00:57:06,620
Yes, sir.

755
00:57:10,620 --> 00:57:12,620
Damn queen.

756
00:57:13,620 --> 00:57:16,620
Born and bred to the field.

757
00:57:17,620 --> 00:57:20,620
Nigger among niggers.

758
00:57:22,620 --> 00:57:24,620
And God gave her to me.

759
00:57:24,620 --> 00:57:29,620
Lesson in the rewards of righteous living.

760
00:57:29,620 --> 00:57:32,620
All be observant to that.

761
00:57:32,620 --> 00:57:34,620
All.

762
00:57:34,620 --> 00:57:38,620
Now, Treech, now speak.

763
00:57:38,620 --> 00:57:42,620
138 pounds for Phoebe.

764
00:57:42,620 --> 00:57:46,620
Hit 145 yesterday. Pull her out.

765
00:57:46,620 --> 00:57:49,620
206 pounds for George.

766
00:57:49,620 --> 00:57:51,620
How much you pick yesterday?

767
00:57:51,620 --> 00:57:53,380
Six pounds for George.

768
00:57:53,380 --> 00:57:56,300
How much you pick yesterday?

769
00:57:56,300 --> 00:57:57,940
2.29.

770
00:57:57,940 --> 00:57:59,100
Get him out.

771
00:57:59,100 --> 00:58:00,000
Come on, get.

772
00:58:02,680 --> 00:58:04,160
Come on.

773
00:58:04,160 --> 00:58:05,180
Come on, boy, move.

774
00:58:21,620 --> 00:58:23,620
No!

775
00:58:51,620 --> 00:59:21,600
Mm-hmm.

776
00:59:21,620 --> 00:59:23,620
Mm-hmm.

777
00:59:23,620 --> 00:59:24,620
Mm-hmm.

778
00:59:24,620 --> 00:59:27,620
Mm-hmm.

779
00:59:27,620 --> 00:59:29,620
Mm-hmm.

780
00:59:29,620 --> 00:59:31,620
Mm-hmm.

781
00:59:31,620 --> 00:59:32,620
Mm-hmm.

782
00:59:51,620 --> 00:59:54,660
Get up!

783
00:59:55,220 --> 00:59:56,180
We danced tonight!

784
00:59:56,360 --> 00:59:56,700
Get up!

785
00:59:57,000 --> 00:59:57,880
Get your fiddle pack!

786
00:59:57,960 --> 00:59:58,280
Get up!

787
00:59:58,560 --> 00:59:58,980
Come on!

788
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:02,000
Come on, Vlad, come on!

789
01:00:02,000 --> 01:00:04,000
Come on!

790
01:00:14,000 --> 01:00:17,000
Come on, where's your merriment? Move your feet!

791
01:00:30,000 --> 01:00:32,160
Sell her.

792
01:00:32,160 --> 01:00:33,660
What's all this?

793
01:00:33,660 --> 01:00:36,200
You will sell the niggers.

794
01:00:36,200 --> 01:00:38,200
Sell little Pats?

795
01:00:38,200 --> 01:00:41,200
She picked with more vigor than any other nigger.

796
01:00:41,200 --> 01:00:42,200
Choose another to go.

797
01:00:42,200 --> 01:00:44,000
No other.

798
01:00:44,000 --> 01:00:45,700
Sell her.

799
01:00:45,700 --> 01:00:48,200
I will not.

800
01:00:48,200 --> 01:00:51,200
You will remove that black bitch from this property,

801
01:00:51,200 --> 01:00:54,200
or I'll take myself back to Cheneyville.

802
01:00:54,200 --> 01:01:01,200
Back to that hog's trough where I found you.

803
01:01:01,200 --> 01:01:07,200
Do not set yourself up against Patsy, my dear.

804
01:01:07,200 --> 01:01:14,200
Because I will rid myself of you well before I do away with her.

805
01:01:14,200 --> 01:01:24,200
What you looking at?

806
01:01:24,200 --> 01:01:26,200
Damn woman.

807
01:01:26,200 --> 01:01:29,200
I won't have my moon spoiled.

808
01:01:29,200 --> 01:01:31,200
I will not.

809
01:01:31,200 --> 01:01:34,200
Dance.

810
01:01:34,200 --> 01:01:36,200
Dance, I said.

811
01:01:40,200 --> 01:01:42,200
Come on.

812
01:01:42,200 --> 01:01:44,200
Pick it up, Quack.

813
01:01:44,200 --> 01:01:46,200
Play that little boy.

814
01:01:46,200 --> 01:01:48,200
Whoo!

815
01:02:12,200 --> 01:02:23,620
Platt.

816
01:02:25,960 --> 01:02:26,680
Yes, Mistress?

817
01:02:29,420 --> 01:02:31,500
Can you find your way to Bartholomew's?

818
01:02:32,580 --> 01:02:33,440
I can, ma'am.

819
01:02:34,360 --> 01:02:36,400
This is a list of goods and sundries.

820
01:02:36,520 --> 01:02:38,480
You will take it to be filled and return immediately.

821
01:02:39,780 --> 01:02:40,700
Take your tag.

822
01:02:40,700 --> 01:02:43,700
Tell Bartholomew to add it to our debt.

823
01:02:43,700 --> 01:02:45,700
Yes, Mistress.

824
01:02:45,700 --> 01:02:48,700
Where you from, Platt?

825
01:02:50,700 --> 01:02:52,700
I told you.

826
01:02:52,700 --> 01:02:54,700
Tell me again.

827
01:02:54,700 --> 01:02:55,700
Washington.

828
01:02:55,700 --> 01:02:56,700
Who were you master?

829
01:02:56,700 --> 01:02:57,700
Master Namor Freeman.

830
01:02:57,700 --> 01:02:59,700
Was he a learned man?

831
01:02:59,700 --> 01:03:01,700
I suppose so.

832
01:03:01,700 --> 01:03:04,700
He learn you to read?

833
01:03:04,700 --> 01:03:07,700
A word, here or there.

834
01:03:07,700 --> 01:03:09,700
But I've no understanding of the written text.

835
01:03:09,700 --> 01:03:11,700
Don't trouble yourself with it.

836
01:03:11,700 --> 01:03:15,700
Same as the rest. Master brought you here to work, that's all.

837
01:03:15,700 --> 01:03:19,700
Any more, I'll earn you a hundred lashes.

